        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "After going back and forth with this feature, I think I am going to close this. At least for the following reasons:\n- 'mini.pick' is already quite big and adding this feature is not as concise as I'd like it to be.\n- The custom picker from previous comment is not *that* big to include in custom config.\n- Similar (and maybe even slightly better) behavior can be achieved with 'mini.visits'. There is a [dedicated `visit_paths()` picker in 'mini.extra'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ecde5ffd9adfd590d5c2d5d35a7f0152def894fc/doc/mini-extra.txt#L740) which can be customized [via `filter` local option](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ecde5ffd9adfd590d5c2d5d35a7f0152def894fc/doc/mini-extra.txt#L760-L761) which can include something like `vim.fn.bufexists(path_data.path) == 1`.",
